make 4.4.1 (GPL-3.0-or-later)

programs/make.wasm is built from the upstream source below, with the changes listed under it. Together they
are the complete corresponding source of the binary; this is the offer of it.

Upstream source
  make-4.4.1.tar.gz  (make 4.4.1, GPL-3.0-or-later)
    sha256 dd16fb1d67bfab79a72f5e8390735c49e3e8e70b4945a15ab1f81ddb78658fb3
    from https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/make/make-4.4.1.tar.gz

Changes and build scripts (in wasm/ of the package, and in the repository under core/utils-copyleft/wasm/)
  wasm/make/build.sh
    the build: configures make to start its jobs with posix_spawn and to wait for jobserver tokens without pselect; the make source is unmodified

The changes were made in 2026; the repository history dates each one.

Toolchain: WALI's musl and the LLVM runtimes (musl 243ec00c3ffb910375db487d7eb24ea76d1e2c9f, LLVM 22.1.8), with the patches in utils/wali/patches;
utils/wali-version in the repository pins them, and utils/wali/build-sysroot.sh builds them. Its compiler then
puts a signal check in each loop of the linked program (utils/wali/signal-checks.mjs).

Where to get it
  - /sources/make-4.4.1.tar.gz on the site that served this program, and the other archives listed above in the same place
  - the sources/ and wasm/ directories of the npm package @ecmaos/coreutils-copyleft, in the version that holds this file
  - https://github.com/ecmaos/ecmaos (core/utils-copyleft), at the tag of the release that holds this file
